# Azure Plugin — runnable .http examples
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. Control Plane API running locally (default: http://localhost:5149)
#   2. Azure__TenantId / Azure__SubscriptionId / Azure__ClientId / Azure__ClientSecret
#      set in .env.local (never commit real values — see SECURITY.md)
#
# Secrets: never commit real tenant IDs, subscription IDs, or client secrets here.
# HOST/PROJECT_ID come from .env by default via {{$dotenv ...}}; override them in
# your local .env.local (gitignored) instead of editing this file.

@HOST = {{$dotenv HOST}}
@PROJECT_ID = {{$dotenv PROJECT_ID}}

###
# Restart an Azure App Service.
# RequiresConfirmation=true — the UI asks for confirmation before executing.
# This is currently a stub: see RestartAppServiceOperation.ExecuteAsync.

POST {{HOST}}/api/operations/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{PROJECT_ID}}",
  "operationId": "restart-app-service",
  "requestedBy": "engineer@example.com",
  "input": {
    "serviceName": "example-app-service"
  }
}

###
# Retrieve the last 20 operation executions (includes Azure plugin history).

GET {{HOST}}/api/operations/history?take=20
Accept: application/json
